From ed7bea5bfede85a194409564036b6d80e5dcaaad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:17:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci parity: universal invocation contracts, full execution
 semantics, pinned legs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The PR #738 audit (7.0/10) adjudicated, re-based on main after the merge.
Every probe was independently reproduced before any edit; all confirmed
defects are closed fail-closed. This revision carries the audit response
onto main as it stands now: PR #738 merged WITHOUT the asmdiff/encdiff
parser half of the series (S15-a was never pushed), and PR #742 landed a
new deep-nesting-robustness gate plus a mode sweep on top — both are
kept, and both are held to the rules this checker enforces.

THE CENTRAL FIX (W1, the audit's P1): INVOCATION_CONTRACTS replaces the
per-gate existential loops. Every command-position invocation of a
contracted program on either mirror must match exactly one registered
contract — exact multisets of option/value pairs, rest tokens AND
environment-assignment prefix, argparse semantics modelled (store is
last-wins, append is a value list, prefix abbreviations like --filt are
not spellings) — and every contract must be matched once per declared
side. A second unpinned asmdiff line (local or hosted), an extra unpinned
encdiff --32, and a filtered or --filt-abbreviated linker run beside the
strict one were exit-0 before and are failures now, with the exact token
diff in the message.

EXECUTION SEMANTICS COMPLETED (W2/W3/W5-W7/W9/W10): job-level if/continue-
on-error and workflow/job/step env merged into the walker; per-program
env-channel guards (GAS_DL_DIR/GAS_CACHE, LCCC*, import-time LCCC_OBJDUMP,
suite channels, LINKTEST_CC/CXX); the tarball sha256 pin enforced on
every ensure_gas trust path; gate registrations parsed from comment-
stripped `gate NAME fast|slow' lines with the speed class pinned; a
closed wrapper grammar (timeout DUR, nice, command, setsid, time, nohup,
env -u/-i, one-deep bash -c judged at payload level; unknown flags fail;
env additions are contract changes); ${VAR}->$VAR canonicalisation with
single-quoted/backslash-$ refusal; a duplicate-key-refusing SafeLoader
subclass; main() aggregates every failing check.

NEW THIS REVISION - workflow `on:' trigger semantics, the same-class
completion of W2 that this re-base's own red-team found: the walker read
step- and job-level conditions but not the WORKFLOW's triggers, so a
schedule-only or dispatch-only workflow hosting a gate counted as hosted
coverage while nothing in it ever ran on a push or pull_request. Those
workflows' bodies are now excluded from parity and their guarded programs
reported ("not coverage"), push/pull_request (any spelling, mixed lists,
branch-filtered mappings) stay active, and _workflow_triggers reads both
`on' spellings because PyYAML resolves the unquoted key to the BOOLEAN
True (YAML 1.1) — a naive doc.get("on") sees nothing for every normally
written workflow. Pinned by 7 new mutation tests (53 -> 60), including
the gotcha itself; neutralizing the guard fails exactly its tests.

SUITE LEGS PINNED (W6): the real-toolchain legs resolve their tools from
explicit channels (ASMDIFF_TEST_AS/ASMDIFF_TEST_OBJDUMP,
ENCDIFF_TEST_OBJDUMP, set by both mirrors to the provisioned 2.47 pair)
and LCCC_REQUIRE_PINNED_ORACLE=1 turns a missing or non-executable pin
into an ERROR, not a skip — re-implemented on main's test files, whose
base revision the parser half of the series never landed on. The local
gates run after provisioning, so the ordering cannot rot: running before
it now fails the gate itself.

Verified on this box against the freshly provisioned pinned 2.47 pair:
checker PASS on the real tree (134 commands, 12 contracts); mutation
suite 60/60 (the guard->test map in the docstring is complete, and the
deletion convention was re-proven empirically for the new guard);
test_asmdiff 19/19 and test_encdiff 66/66 bare AND pinned+require, with
require-mode proven to error on both missing and non-executable pins;
ensure_gas self-test 15/15; bash -n both shell files; workflow-shell,
script-imports, no-conflict-markers and pipefail-sigpipe gates green;
the five tooling gates green through ci_local.sh --only. The audit's
bypass repros re-run on this tree: dropping the deep-nesting step or
gate from either mirror, a malformed speed class, a second unpinned
asmdiff/encdiff invocation, and a schedule-only workflow hosting the
only copy of a gate all fail with their exact diffs. The deep-nesting
gate's mirror difference (--lccc "$LCCC" locally, the workflow's default
target/fastbuild/lccc hosted) is adjudicated legitimate: the compiler is
the artifact under test, not an oracle; presence and speed parity for
that gate are enforced (proven by mutation).
